  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 1232 PM MDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nNot much change in the forecast for most of next week. High pressure \nwill remain in place overhead, along with light winds and relatively \ndry air. Latest guidance shows some isolated to scattered afternoon \nshowers over the mountains on Tuesday as a weak disturbance rolls \nthrough, but otherwise the area is expected to stay mostly dry. \nTemperatures will remain warm, with highs consistently in the 70s-\n80s over most of our CWA. \n\nModel consistency starts to break down as we head into next weekend. \nGeneral consensus is for a brief cooling trend to set in, with hints \nat active weather after that, though the details are still far from \ncertain.",
